# Manyhalls fleet supervisor — one firing (Proofdelve ForgeOs-dx34.4, spec section 4
# layer 3). Drafted and installed under Regent edict 2026-09-10, gate 6, with
# the Overseer's signature recorded on the bead; installed by hand into
# ~/.config/systemd/user/ — this file does nothing where it lives in the repo.
#
# Each firing runs fort/scripts/fleet-supervisor.sh once. Its header is the
# design; in one line: halt file -> nothing; run live -> exit 75, silent but
# COUNTED in $FLEET_STATE/supervisor.streak; nothing fleet-safe -> nothing;
# otherwise start a run as its own transient unit (manyhalls-fleet-run-<id>)
# and exit at once.
#
# EXIT 75 IS SUCCESS HERE, BY DESIGN (criterion 3): it is the normal outcome
# of firing during a live run, and a unit that went "failed" forty times over
# an eighty-minute run would train its reader to ignore `--failed`. The two
# exits that DO fail the unit are 64s: a masked launch, bd not answering, or
# a run that could not be started — each with one stderr line in the journal.
#
# WHY THIS IS NOT Type=simple WITH THE FLEET AS ITS MAIN PROCESS: the timer
# will not start a unit that is already active, so a service that lasted the
# whole run would never fire DURING one, and the streak could never count. The
# fleet runs in its own unit instead; see the supervisor's header.
#
# A firing under a halt file is a no-op, which is how the first night was made
# safe: the halt file stayed in place overnight and the Overseer removed it
# while watching. That removal is the recorded first unattended pickup.

[Unit]
Description=Manyhalls fleet supervisor — start a fleet run when work appears

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=/home/justin/dev/fortkit
# User units do not inherit a login shell PATH. bd and claude live in
# ~/.local/bin; node, npm and codex under nvm. THIS IS THE ONE LIST (Proofdelve ForgeOs-eedj):
# the supervisor forwards its own $PATH to each fleet run it starts and
# resolves the run's tools on it first, so a node upgrade that breaks this line
# refuses in the journal instead of presenting as a Forge that never starts.
# Edit here; the installed copy under ~/.config/systemd/user/ is the Overseer's
# to refresh (systemctl --user daemon-reload after copying).
Environment=PATH=/home/justin/.local/bin:/home/justin/.nvm/versions/node/v24.14.0/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
ExecStart=/home/justin/dev/fortkit/fort/scripts/fleet-supervisor.sh
SuccessExitStatus=75
# One bd query and one flock probe; anything longer is bd hanging.
TimeoutStartSec=2min
